{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Progress/root cause: confirmed the composed trap spans (1) plan-review P4 using raw description length for admission, so an AC correction can invalidate the prior attestation and make the required re-review inadmissible, and (2) completion_precheck treating the same 8,000-char review admission cap as a deterministic close failure. Current exposure from the fetched ticket store: 18 open/in-progress work tickets are within 200 chars below the 8,000 raw-description cap. Implementing the narrow fix in fresh worktree fix7-agama: charge P4/save-time warning only for review-bounded prose outside ## Acceptance Criteria, keep AC count + P8 whole-context budget as the AC-side bounds, and remove the completion-verifier description-cap close criterion."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788816278397973001,"uuid":"d7548b95-034c-4c77-92b7-3ad45e7a9406"}